---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About MyRigFoundry | PC Troubleshooting & Hardware Guides"
  description="Learn what MyRigFoundry is about and how we create practical PC troubleshooting, hardware and upgrade guides."
>
  <section class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT MYRIGFOUNDRY</p>

      <h1>PC problems shouldn't feel impossible to solve.</h1>

      <p class="info-lead">
        MyRigFoundry is a practical PC troubleshooting and hardware
        publication built to help people understand what is happening
        inside their computer, fix problems step by step, and make better
        upgrade decisions.
      </p>

      <div class="info-content">
        <h2>What we do</h2>

        <p>
          PC problems are often explained with either too little information
          or far more complexity than most people actually need.
        </p>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry focuses on clear troubleshooting guides for real
          problems involving Windows, performance, storage, networking,
          memory, BIOS settings, graphics cards, monitors and other PC
          hardware.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our goal is not just to tell you which setting to change. We want
          to explain what the problem may mean, how to narrow down the cause,
          and what to try next.
        </p>

        <h2>Understand it. Fix it. Upgrade it.</h2>

        <p>
          That idea defines how MyRigFoundry approaches PC problems.
        </p>

        <div class="info-principles">
          <div class="info-principle">
            <span>01</span>

            <div>
              <h3>Understand it</h3>

              <p>
                Learn what the symptoms actually tell you before changing
                random settings or replacing hardware.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-principle">
            <span>02</span>

            <div>
              <h3>Fix it</h3>

              <p>
                Follow practical troubleshooting steps in an order that
                helps eliminate possible causes.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-principle">
            <span>03</span>

            <div>
              <h3>Upgrade it</h3>

              <p>
                When hardware really is the limitation, understand what an
                upgrade would solve before spending money.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>How our guides are created</h2>

        <p>
          We start with problems that PC users are actually experiencing.
          From there, we research the issue, compare possible explanations,
          consult official documentation and technical resources, and build
          a troubleshooting path around the most useful tests.
        </p>

        <p>
          When a guide references manufacturer or operating-system
          documentation, we aim to link directly to those official resources
          so readers can verify important technical information themselves.
        </p>

        <h2>Our approach to recommendations</h2>

        <p>
          Buying new hardware should not be the first answer to every PC
          problem.
        </p>

        <p>
          When troubleshooting can solve an issue, that comes first. When an
          upgrade genuinely makes sense, we aim to explain why it may help,
          what specifications matter and what limitations to consider.
        </p>

        <h2>Built for curious PC users</h2>

        <p>
          You do not need to be a hardware engineer to understand your own
          computer.
        </p>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry is being built as a growing reference library for PC
          users who want explanations that are useful, focused and easy to
          follow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>